                                                                Experiment-4 
A) Middle of the Linked List
B) palindrome Linked List

    AIM (A) - Given the head of a singly linked list, return the middle node of the linked list.
     If there are two middle nodes, return the second middle node.

ALGORITHM- 

1. Start two pointers, slow and fast, at the head of the linked list.
2. Move slow one node at a time.
3. Move fast two nodes at a time.
4. Continue this process while:

  fast != NULL && fast->next != NULL

5. When fast reaches the end of the linked list, slow will be at the middle node.
6. Return slow.
7. For an even number of nodes, this method automatically returns the second middle node.

CODE- 
class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* middleNode(ListNode* head) {

        ListNode* slow = head;
        ListNode* fast = head;

        while (fast != nullptr && fast->next != nullptr) {

            slow = slow->next;
            fast = fast->next->next;
        }

        return slow;
    }
};

                                  AIM(B)- Given the head of a singly linked list, return true if it is a palindrome or false otherwise.

ALGORITHM- Using Stack

1. Create an empty stack st.
2. Set a temporary pointer temp to head.
3. Traverse the entire linked list:
       Push each node's value into the stack.
       Move temp to the next node.
4. Reset temp back to head.
5. Traverse the linked list again:
       Compare temp->val with st.top().
       If they are different, return false.
       If they are the same, pop the top element from the stack.
       Move temp to the next node.
6. If all values match, return true.

CODE-
class Solution {
public:
    bool isPalindrome(ListNode* head) {

        stack<int> st;

        ListNode* temp = head;

        while (temp != NULL) {
            st.push(temp->val);
            temp = temp->next;
        }

       
        temp = head;

        while (temp != NULL) {

            if (temp->val != st.top()) {
                return false;
            }

            st.pop();
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        return true;
    }
};
